97, D:latest_bot_tag_state@226-233, D:_actionable_change_key@283-286, D:_refuse_retired_word@308-313, D:handle_comment_added@353-361, C:module@51-55, C:module@62-64, C:module@67-69, C:module@76-79, C:module@115-118, C:module@121-124, C:_refusal_message@256-258, C:module@271-273, C:handle_comment_added@426-430.\n- voter.py (25): D:module@1-22, D:in_flight_reviews@97-104, D:_voter_error@136-139, D:_publish_voter_error_metric@159-163, D:_publish_token_usage_metrics@189-195, D:_emit_token_usage@215-220, D:_extract@238-242, D:review_and_vote@272-283, D:_decision_for_clone@300-308, D:_guard_decision_auth@400-403, D:_resolve_review_runtime@413-416, D:_handle_retryable_gap@429-433, D:_superseded_before_vote@511-518, C:module@64-71, C:module@75-92, C:module@175-178, C:_decision_for_clone@323-326, C:_review_and_vote@616-623, C:_review_and_vote@633-636, C:_review_and_vote@663-666, C:_review_and_vote@701-708, C:_review_and_vote@712-715, C:_review_and_vote@727-730, C:_review_and_vote@765-767, C:_review_and_vote@775-783.\n\n## Contracts, consumers, and exclusions\nPreserve optional-import boundaries; four-pass verdict/coverage mapping; reviewed-tree-to-vote binding; header-first authentication; fast ACK, bounded drain/cancel, and hard-exit sequencing; cursor low-water recovery; merge-delta REST behavior; token redaction; the shared low-disk no-vote route; privileged retrigger eligibility/reset; pre-vote staleness suppression; and post-vote artifact capture. Consumers include the FastAPI service, Gerrit REST, autodeploy/observability scripts, and review-bot tests. The health, webhook, and rerun route docstrings are excluded because FastAPI publishes them through OpenAPI.\n\nConcise/load-bearing prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values, and all 25 directive/shebang physical lines. All files are Python.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base and final Python with `type_comments=True`; replace only allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context base-to-final hunk guard restricts every deletion/insertion to an exact allowlisted base span. Run all six structured DD commands, including exact one-commit paths, focused consumers, scoped diff integrity, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 142 PASS rows, one per stable ID: `stable_id,before_citation,final_citation,preserved_contract_or_consumer,directives_exact,before_words,final_words,reviewer_session,semantic_pass,bloat_pass`. Every `final_words` is smaller; missing, extra, duplicate, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly 142 allowlisted blocks have smaller final word counts.\n- [ ] Non-allowlisted prose and all 25 directive/shebang lines remain exact.\n- [ ] The immutable-base runtime/non-comment oracle passes for every owned file.\n- [ ] Every preserved contract or consumer has an independent TSV PASS citation.\n- [ ] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 10 declared paths and focused, diff-integrity, and hygiene checks exit 0.\n- [ ] Untimed worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788626876948038933,"uuid":"4376f583-5fa0-4e82-8054-61b11c6d8bda"}